---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";

const title = "Terms of Service";
const description =
  "Terms of Service for MorseCodeGenerator.com. Rules for using the site, disclaimers, and limitations of liability.";
const canonical = "https://morsecodegenerator.com/terms/";
const robots = "index,follow";

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "morsecodegenerator@gmail.com";
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "2026-01-28";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} robots={robots}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="muted">
      Effective date: <span class="mono">{EFFECTIVE_DATE}</span>
    </p>

    <p>
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your use of <strong>MorseCodeGenerator.com</strong> (the “Service”).
      By using the Service, you agree to these Terms.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Use of the Service</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You may use the Service for personal or educational purposes.</li>
      <li>You agree not to misuse the Service, attempt to break it, or interfere with normal operation.</li>
      <li>You agree not to use the Service for unlawful activities.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>No warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided “as is” and “as available” without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We do not guarantee that the
      Service will be error-free, uninterrupted, or always available.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Morse code conversions are provided for convenience and learning. While we aim for correctness, you are responsible for verifying
      output before relying on it in any situation where accuracy matters.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages,
      or any loss of data, profits, or revenue arising from your use of the Service.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Advertising and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may display advertisements (e.g., Google AdSense) and use analytics (e.g., Google Analytics). These providers may collect
      information under their own policies. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Site design, text, and code are owned by us or licensed to us, unless otherwise stated. You may not copy, reproduce, or distribute
      substantial portions of the Service without permission, except as allowed by law.
    </p>

    <h2>User content</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us feedback or suggestions, you grant us the right to use them without restriction or compensation.
      The translator input you type is processed in your browser; we do not claim ownership of your input.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No attempts to probe, scan, or test vulnerabilities.</li>
      <li>No automated scraping that materially impacts site performance.</li>
      <li>No malicious content, malware, or abuse.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes and termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may update or discontinue parts of the Service at any time. We may restrict access if we believe the Service is being abused.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by applicable laws in the jurisdiction where the Service operator is based, without regard to conflict of law
      principles.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms? Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
